WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.980
- Here's a question.

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:04.440
If you could switch
places with one person,

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.273
you love your life.

00:00:05.273 --> 00:00:06.106
There's nothing wrong with you.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:06.939
You're great.

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:07.910
But if you could switch places

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:09.960
with one person who would it be?

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.740
- Oh my goodness.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:14.750
I would...

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.767
I would switch places with
Elon Musk and I would do-

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:20.600
- Oh my god!

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:21.433
That's mine!

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:23.490
I am obsessed!

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.760
I've read like books on him.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:25.593
I'm obsessed!

00:00:25.593 --> 00:00:26.480
I think he's so cool.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.064
That's mine.

00:00:28.064 --> 00:00:29.770
- Me too!

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:31.080
- [Kelly] I think he's so interesting.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.133
I want my brain to work like that.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:35.300
- I want my brain to work like that

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.040
but I also want like
still part of my brain

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:41.350
that would spend money in an incredibly

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.360
like different, creative
way than perhaps amazing,

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.328
brilliant Elon Musk would spend it.

00:00:47.328 --> 00:00:50.230
And I would still only
spend like, you know,

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.500
a billion in a day probably.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.333
- Yeah, I know.

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.491
Isn't it just rough?

00:00:54.491 --> 00:00:55.820
(Kelly chuckles)

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.270
No, I think it's amazing too.

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.491
All the things like innovative
weird kind of things,

00:00:59.491 --> 00:01:00.780
you know, we'll come out with something

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.048
like kind of strange
and you're like, "What?"

00:01:02.048 --> 00:01:04.150
But I think all those weird things,

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:05.760
they always lead to something amazing.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.790
Like, you know, I'm so excited

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:11.020
about what they're doing
with space and, you know,

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.640
and how he talks about, you know

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.020
AI and like all that stuff.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:15.870
I think it's so interesting.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.075
It's so funny you picked him!

00:01:17.075 --> 00:01:18.464
That would be who I'd pick.

00:01:18.464 --> 00:01:20.858
- That is funny because

00:01:20.858 --> 00:01:23.440
he's been on my mind and I did, well,

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.450
I actually haven't read a bunch of books

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:26.507
but I started reading a book about him

00:01:26.507 --> 00:01:28.370
and it is fascinating.

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:30.420
And it's really funny that
you picked him as well.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.443
See, now you've got to come on my show.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.217
- Well, you know, I'll give
honest raw answers, ma'am.

00:01:37.217 --> 00:01:38.540
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:39.400
- [Minnie] That's what I like.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.772
- My mom is like, "You can
use a tiny bit of a filter,"

00:01:41.772 --> 00:01:43.037
and I'm like, "Why?"

